# Shared settings. Sourced by every script in scripts/.
# Change IMAGE here when testing a new build; nothing else needs editing.
#
# Every value is written `${NAME:-default}` so the environment wins over the
# file. That is not decoration: `source config.env` runs AFTER the shell has
# applied a `VAR=x ./scripts/foo.sh` prefix, so a plain assignment silently
# overwrites the override — soak.sh documented `SOAK_SECONDS=300 ./scripts/soak.sh`
# and ran for 1800s anyway. It also makes the config matrix possible without
# editing this file between runs:
#
#   UBATCH=2048 NP=2 ./scripts/correctness.sh

IMAGE="${IMAGE:-ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp:server-intel-b10630}"
MODELS_DIR="${MODELS_DIR:-/mnt/ssd5/apps/llama-embed}"
MODEL="${MODEL:-/models/Qwen3-Embedding-8B-Q4_K_M.gguf}"

# Production endpoint (the running TrueNAS app).
# TrueNAS 26 has no 127.0.0.1 entry for `localhost` — getent returns ::1 only,
# and the IPv6 docker-proxy resets the connection. Use the literal v4 address.
PROD_URL="${PROD_URL:-http://127.0.0.1:30436}"

# Ports used by throwaway test containers. Must not collide with PROD.
PORT_A="${PORT_A:-30437}"   # production settings
PORT_B="${PORT_B:-30438}"   # reduced-ubatch reference

# Production inference settings under test.
CTX="${CTX:-32768}"
NP="${NP:-4}"
UBATCH="${UBATCH:-8192}"
# Extra llama-server flags appended to every container the harness starts.
# The matrix uses this for things with no dedicated variable (-fa off, -t N).
EXTRA_FLAGS="${EXTRA_FLAGS:-}"
# Extra `docker run -e` settings, space separated. Passed into every container
# the gate and the sweeps start, so they test the environment the app actually
# deploys with.
EXTRA_ENV="${EXTRA_ENV:-GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_DNN=0}"

# Reference settings for the correctness gate. Deliberately conservative:
# small enough to sit well below the #26206 threshold.
REF_UBATCH="${REF_UBATCH:-2048}"
REF_CTX="${REF_CTX:-8192}"
REF_NP="${REF_NP:-1}"

# Correctness thresholds.
MIN_COSINE="${MIN_COSINE:-0.999}"      # production vs reference, per chunk
# Same config, same input, repeated. Much tighter than the cross-config bar:
# this one only has to absorb float noise, not a change of batch geometry.
# MEASURED on B70 / b10630, three full gate runs: every chunk of 1024 tokens
# or more comes back bit-identical, and only the 512-token chunks drift, at
# 0.9999955 worst. That is the documented dispatch boundary — below the
# oneMKL FA floor (K->ne[1] >= 1024) prefill falls to oneDNN SDPA, and that
# path is not bit-reproducible run to run. 1e-5 of drift on identical input
# cannot move a retrieval ranking; #26206 corruption lands far below 0.99.
# 0.9999 sits between the two with two orders of magnitude of margin on
# each side. Tighten it and the gate flaps on noise.
DET_MIN_COSINE="${DET_MIN_COSINE:-0.9999}"

# Passes for the bit-exactness check in correctness.sh. Bit exactness is a
# compliance parameter for a new release, not only a curiosity: cosine says a
# build computes the same function, this says it computes it the same way.
BIT_EXACT_PASSES="${BIT_EXACT_PASSES:-4}"

# The gate pool: boundary-straddling lengths, fast enough to run every time.
FIXTURES="${FIXTURES:-fixtures/chunks.json}"
# The bench pool: real chunk-length distribution, for throughput numbers that
# mean something. Consistency uses FIXTURES; performance uses this.
BENCH_FIXTURES="${BENCH_FIXTURES:-fixtures/bench.json}"

# Soak test duration in seconds.
SOAK_SECONDS="${SOAK_SECONDS:-1800}"
